 128:../Src/system_py32e407.c **** /**
 129:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****    * @brief  Update SystemCoreClock variable according to Clock Register Values.
 130:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         The SystemCoreClock variable contains the core clock (HCLK), it can
 131:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         be used by the user application to setup the SysTick timer or configure
 132:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         other parameters.
 133:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           
 134:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   * @note   Each time the core clock (HCLK) changes, this function must be called
 135:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         to update SystemCoreClock variable value. Otherwise, any configuration
 136:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         based on this variable will be incorrect.         
 137:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *     
 138:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   * @note   - The system frequency computed by this function is not the real 
 139:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           frequency in the chip. It is calculated based on the predefined 
 140:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           constant and the selected clock source:
 141:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *             
 142:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSI_VALUE(*)
 143:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *                                              
 144:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSE, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**)
 145:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *                          
 146:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is PLL, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**) 
 147:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *             or HSI_VALUE(*) multiplied/divided by the PLL factors.
 148:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         
 149:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         (*) HSI_VALUE is a constant defined in py32e407_hal_conf.h file (default value
 150:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *             16 MHz) but the real value may vary depending on the variations
 151:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *             in voltage and temperature.   
 152:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *    
 153:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         (**) HSE_VALUE is a constant defined in py32e407_hal_conf.h file (its value
 154:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *              depends on the application requirements), user has to ensure that HSE_VALUE
 155:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *              is same as the real frequency of the crystal used. Otherwise, this function
 156:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *              may have wrong result.
 157:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *                
 158:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *         - The result of this function could be not correct when using fractional
 159:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *           value for HSE crystal.
 160:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   *     
 161:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   * @param  None
 162:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   * @retval None
 163:../Src/system_py32e407.c ****   */
 164:../Src/system_py32e407.c **** void SystemCoreClockUpdate(void)
 165:../Src/system_py32e407.c **** {
